    "min": 2.6,
    "max": 2.6
  },
  "explanation": "To find the output of the SQL query:<br><br><strong>Step 1:</strong> Count the number of employees in each department by grouping the <code>EMP</code> relation by <code>DeptName</code>:<br>- <strong>AA:</strong> 4 employees (EmpId 1, 2, 3, 4)<br>- <strong>AB:</strong> 3 employees (EmpId 5, 6, 7)<br>- <strong>AC:</strong> 3 employees (EmpId 8, 9, 10)<br>- <strong>AD:</strong> 2 employees (EmpId 11, 12)<br>- <strong>AE:</strong> 1 employee (EmpId 13)<br><br><strong>Step 2:</strong> Calculate the average count of employees per department (<code>AVG(EC.Num)</code>):<br>Total number of employees = $4 + 3 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 13$<br>Total number of distinct departments = $5$<br><br>$$\\text{Average} = \\frac{13}{5} = 2.6$$<br><br>Hence, the output of the query is <strong>2.6</strong>.",
